<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego Silang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1730–<a href="/years/1763">1763</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego Silang was the leader of a revolt in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilocos">Ilocos</a> region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a> against Spanish rule during the British occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>. Declaring himself a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the British, he took Vigan in 1762, but he was assassinated in May 1763 by men in Spanish pay. His wife, Gabriela Silang, continued the revolt until she was captured and executed.</p></div>
